{"schema":"ntui-app-v1","generatedUtc":"2026-10-24T02:46:28.485Z","dataThrough":"2026-10-23","thesis":"Are the native tokens (CC, LINK) actually used by the systems and companies making tokenization claims?","verdicts":[{"token":"CC","verdict":"INCONCLUSIVE","label":"MIXED","plain":"Some token demand, but not enough to call it.","color":"amber","reason":"Coverage, trend or completeness does not meet a decisive rule.","supporting":[],"contradicting":["30d burn coverage 0.670 (burned / minted).","90d burn trend FLAT (ratio 0.96)."],"gaps":["Source is Lighthouse (lighthouse.xyz), a third-party ETL of Canton Scan; official Scan returns 403 to non-validator IPs.","Dedicated synchronizers are NOT_OBSERVABLE in Scan (structural; CIP-0129 is APPROVED_NOT_IMPLEMENTED).","Holding-fee expiry burns (Amulet_Expire*) are counted but their amount is NOT_OBSERVABLE.","Minted excludes dev-fund mint (about 5% of issuance; not served per day), so coverage is overstated by up to ~5%.","2 day(s) of burns are LOWER_BOUND (top-50 cap); NOT_SUPPORTED is blocked."]},{"token":"LINK","verdict":"NOT_SUPPORTED","label":"NO","plain":"Usage is not turning into demand for the token.","color":"red","reason":"CCIP mainnet activity rose (x1.54) while measured LINK demand did not keep pace: 90d Reserve inflow 1,306,859 LINK is under 10% of the 18,750,000 LINK released. Fee-token use is NOT_OBSERVABLE, so LINK paid directly as CCIP fees is not counted.","supporting":["30d Reserve inflow 422,894 LINK."],"contradicting":["Reserve inflows FALLING over 90d (ratio 0.88).","30d inflow 422,894 vs 30d LINK released 18,750,000 from official non-circulating wallets.","CCIP mainnet activity RISING (ratio 1.54) - usage growth to compare against inflows."],"gaps":["CCIP per-message fee token is NOT_OBSERVABLE via the REST API; LINK is not required to pay CCIP fees.","Reserve inflows do not show which customer or product the converted revenue came from."]}],"questions":[{"id":"cc_burn","token":"CC","question":"Is Canton Coin being used up as fast as new coins are created?","answer":"For every 100 new CC created in the last 30 days, about 67 were burned (used up paying for the network). Creation is ahead of burning, so supply is still growing.","number":67,"unit":"burned per 100 created"},{"id":"cc_who","token":"CC","question":"Who is actually burning Canton Coin?","answer":"Three accounts (temple-mainnet-1, kora-mainNetValidator-1, cantor8-digik-1) did 78.7% of all burning. None of the banks or institutions in the tokenization claims appears among the top 50 burners.","number":78.7,"unit":"% of burn by top 3"},{"id":"cc_rewards","token":"CC","question":"Is the burning paid for by the network's own rewards?","answer":"0% of the burning comes from accounts that earn at least as much in app rewards as they burn, so it pays for itself. 30.2% comes from accounts that mostly pay out of pocket.","number":0,"unit":"% reward-funded"},{"id":"link_reserve","token":"LINK","question":"Is Chainlink revenue buying LINK faster than new LINK is released?","answer":"For every 100 LINK released from Chainlink's locked supply in the last 90 days, about 7 went into the Chainlink Reserve. Reserve inflows are falling.","number":7,"unit":"into Reserve per 100 released"},{"id":"link_usage","token":"LINK","question":"Is the Chainlink network (CCIP) being used more?","answer":"Yes: cross-chain messages were 54% higher in the second half of the last 90 days than the first. 62,674 messages in the last 30 days. Usage growing while token demand is not is the gap the thesis is about.","number":54,"unit":"% usage growth"}],"blindSpots":["Private Canton networks (where most bank tokenization runs) burn no CC today, so their use cannot show up here. CIP-0129 (approved Oct 21, 2026; expected around Q1 2027) would change that.","Account names are chosen by their operators. A bank running through a vendor's node shows the vendor's name.","The CCIP fee token is read only for messages sent from Ethereum, the busiest